@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
allowmixing
title MVP + EXPLICIT FUTURE PATHS — Proposed — Consumers, owner contracts and external adapters
!pragma useVerticalIf on
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor "Private browser / scoped employer viewer" as B
component "Selected HTTP entry / transport mapping\nnot a separately selected API gateway" as H
component "Resource owner\ncurrent scope / lifecycle / invariants" as O
interface "Explicit owner operation\nprovided" as P
interface "Required scoped capability" as R
component "MVP private storage adapter; provider / executor AFTER MVP" as A
component "Other in-process module" as C
B --> H : candidate same-origin HTTPS
H --> P
C --> P : language-level contract, no invented HTTP hop
O - P
O --> R
A ..|> R
note bottom of O
 Public module contract is not automatically public internet API.
 Git clients use actual native Git transport, not a generic JSON envelope.
 No GraphQL/gRPC/broker/gateway service adopted here.
end note

@enduml
